  "_notes": {
    "abbreviations": "МПС = motor vehicle; ППС = road vehicle; ПТП = road traffic accident; ЗДвП = Road Traffic Act; ППЗДвП = Rules for Implementing the Road Traffic Act; МВР = Ministry of the Interior; КАТ = Traffic Police; ИААА = Executive Agency “Automobile Administration”; ЕО = EC; ЕС = EU; ДВГ = internal combustion engine; ТОЛ = toll; ЕКМТ/СЕМТ = ECMT; ТИР = TIR; УПК = CPC (certificate of professional competence). Latin acronyms (ABS, ESP, ASR, BUS, IRU, LED, ADR, CMR, TIR) stay as written. All Bulgarian abbreviations are written out in full, except ECMT, TIR, CPC, EC and EU, which are the standard English abbreviations.",
    "citations": "“чл. 157, ал. 4 ЗДвП” = “Art. 157(4) of the Road Traffic Act”; “т. 3” = point 3, written “Art. 6(1)(3)” style only when the full chain is given.",
    "yes_no": "да/не = yes/no; правилно/неправилно = correct/incorrect; вярно/невярно = true/false; разрешено/забранено = permitted/prohibited. Lower case, as in Bulgarian.",
    "units": "SI symbols kept: km/h, km, m, cm, mm, kg, t, kW, V, A, ‰, %, °C, bar, l (litre), h (hour), min, s. Decimal point “.” (3,5 т = 3.5 t). Thousands grouped with a comma only where the Bulgarian groups them. 24-hour clock. Dates keep their digits.",
    "quotation_marks": "“ ” (English typographic double quotes), ‘ ’ for quotes inside quotes. Sign names in quotes keep the Bulgarian sign name translated: знак „Стоп“ = the “Stop” sign.",
    "licence_categories": "Official Latin codes AM, A1, A2, A, B1, B, BE, C1, C1E, C, CE, D1, D1E, D, DE; national Tkt, Ttb, Ttm. Bus classes: class A/B, classes I, II, III.",
    "picture_labels": "A letter marking something in a picture is written with the visually identical Latin letter (А = A, В = B, С = C, Е = E, Н = H, К = K, М = M, О = O, Р = P, Т = T, Х = X, а = a, е = e, о = o, р = p, с = c, х = x). Letters with no Latin look-alike are kept as shown in the picture and recorded in notes.md.",
    "car_vs_vehicle": "автомобил is a motor vehicle with at least four wheels (lorries, buses and trolleybuses included). Default “car” (traffic situations, rules, pictures, colloquial vehicle types: “автомобил и ремарке” = a car and a trailer, where “vehicle” would make a wrong answer right). “automobile” where the legal category itself is tested (iaaa-5324…5329: the correct pictures are a lorry, a trolleybus and a van; iaaa-5177/5178), because “car” would make those correct answers wrong. “vehicle” where the question is about the vehicle's own systems, parts and maintenance (T01, T03, T04, T11 …) or where автомобил plainly includes heavy vehicles in a definition (iaaa-11823, 7848). превозно средство = vehicle; ППС = road vehicle; МПС = motor vehicle; лек автомобил = passenger car; товарен автомобил = goods vehicle.",
    "driver_rider": "водач = driver; for a motorcycle, moped or bicycle it is “rider”. A generic водачите (all vehicles) is “drivers”.",
    "stopping_standing_parking": "спиране = stopping (any stop); престой = standing (the Vienna Convention term for a stop only for the time needed to let people on or off or to load or unload); паркиране = parking.",
    "overtaking_going_around_passing": "изпреварване = overtaking (same direction, moving); заобикаляне = going around (a stationary vehicle or an obstacle); разминаване = passing (an oncoming vehicle). “pass” is reserved for разминаване where the distinction matters; минавам/преминавам = go past / go through / cross.",
    "road_classes": "автомагистрала = motorway; скоростен път = expressway; автомобилен път = road for motor vehicles (the official English name of Vienna Convention sign E,6a, white car on blue: closed to mopeds, tractors and bicycles, no U-turns or reversing, 90 km/h outside built-up areas). Not “motor road”, which plain English hardly distinguishes from “motorway”. Three road classes, three distinct terms (review wave 2).",
    "carriageway_roadway":"The bank distinguishes платно за движение (carriageway) from пътно платно (roadway) as different answers (iaaa-11579, iaaa-11580), so they get different English words.",
    "amber_yellow": "жълт is “amber” for light signals (traffic lights, flashing lights) and “yellow” for the colour of objects (markings, vehicles, plates).",
    "modality": "длъжен е / задължен е / трябва = must (is obliged to); може = may (permission) or can (possibility); има право = is entitled to; разрешено е = is permitted; забранено е / не се разрешава = is prohibited / is not permitted; препоръчително е = is advisable.",
    "address": "The candidate is addressed with “you”, in the neutral formal register of UK theory-test questions."
  }
}
